WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.476
A lot of the work people want automated lives on their computer.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.431
Behind a sign-in. In an app with no API.

00:00:09.431 --> 00:00:10.897
In an Excel file.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.569
Now those jobs are yours.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:21.253
Describe the job, and Kitewell lays out every step for you to check.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.866
Prefer code?

00:00:23.866 --> 00:00:26.077
It's plain YAML.

00:00:26.077 --> 00:00:27.711
Build it from Claude Code or Codex, over MCP.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:33.003
It runs on their computer, and their passwords stay there.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.397
It does the clicking: websites, desktop apps, and email.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:44.302
It stops for their OK where it matters, and keeps a record of every step.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.295
Got a list in Excel? It runs for every row, and writes each result back beside it.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.330
It learns the clicks once, replays them without the model, and relearns when a page changes.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.021
If a run fails, the alert names the step, in your Slack.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.556
Fix it on your laptop, and the fix reaches their computer.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.770
What you teach goes into the project's notes, for whoever takes over.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.170
You build it. Their computers do the work.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.250
Kitewell.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.100
It flies on its own.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.036
You hold the string.
